      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bcgu",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scgt",
          "text": "The owners and managers of the buildings where you live, work, and shop are generally required to maintain safe premises so you don’t get hurt on their properties. Part of this responsibility includes fixing any parts of the property that are in disrepair or are on their way to it. When such maintenance isn’t carried out, damaged and/or unsafe features on properties can cause serious accidents and injuries.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bcgw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scgv",
          "text": "At Dormer Harpring, our lawyers know how to prove when negligent building maintenance has caused accidents and injuries. Effective at protecting our clients in any legal setting, we are ready to help you get onto the path to recovery following an accident on someone else’s property.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bcgy",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "scgx",
          "text": "Common Examples of Negligent Building Maintenance",
          "marks": []
